    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1386">

                <pb facs="1182" n="1078" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1078"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11D29/45.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 498.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-08-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 11, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the disturbances which
                    took place in the city of Panama on July 4, 1912, I have the honor to inform you
                    that I have been informed by Señor Lefevre, the Minister for Foreign Affairs,
                    that the Panaman Government has already arrested seven <pb facs="1183" n="1079"
                        xml:id="pg1079"/> officers of the police force who are believed to have been
                    concerned in the riot, and is pursuing an investigation, a report upon which has
                    been promised to me within a very short time.</p>
                <p>In view of the noticeable delay on the part of the Panaman Government in pursuing
                    this matter I have vigorously urged with Señor Lefevre that it be given
                    immediate attention and that the report be prepared as quickly as possible
                    setting forth the attitude and proposed action of the Panaman Government in
                    adjusting this affair along the lines indicated by the Department.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cyrus F. Wicker</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
